{"agency_id": "courts-nz", "canonical_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724734254534665", "captured_at": "2021-04-10T03:30:29+00:00", "content": "An investiture ceremony was held today for Justice Joe Williams at Manaia Marae on the Coromandel Peninsula. Speakers included Governor-General Dame Patsy Reddy, Chief Justice Helen Winkelmann, and Tā Joe. Sir Joe’s many and varied accomplishments were celebrated. pic.twitter.com/tm9QmhhHdu", "content_hash": "634a8c1c6d3c729bf5ec1eb26ac7d975cefe1410349bae0a6bcdbb7356dd8f58", "cross_source_ids": {"archive_month": "2021-04", "tweet_id": "1380724734254534665"}, "extraction_method": "internet_archive_cdx_plus_x_oembed", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2021-04-10T00:00:00+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw/x/2021-04/1380724734254534665.json", "record_id": "x:1380724734254534665", "source_account": "CourtsofNZ", "source_kind": "inactive_social_archive", "source_platform": "x", "source_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724734254534665"}
{"agency_id": "courts-nz", "canonical_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724739568664581", "captured_at": "2021-04-10T03:30:37+00:00", "content": "Chief Justice Winkelmann said that Tā Joe “is fierce in his passion to build a just society, and in his belief that the law can and should play a part in building that society”.", "content_hash": "9f9e596c80facadf1bebaf56fd812019cfbf71bd1955b0b58393c94b66f7fb6d", "cross_source_ids": {"archive_month": "2021-04", "tweet_id": "1380724739568664581"}, "extraction_method": "internet_archive_cdx_plus_x_oembed", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2021-04-10T00:00:00+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw/x/2021-04/1380724739568664581.json", "record_id": "x:1380724739568664581", "source_account": "CourtsofNZ", "source_kind": "inactive_social_archive", "source_platform": "x", "source_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724739568664581"}
{"agency_id": "courts-nz", "canonical_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724743494504451", "captured_at": "2021-04-10T03:30:47+00:00", "content": "Her Honour “wholeheartedly supports” Sir Joe’s vision “for a society in which iwi are given the space to use their wisdom and manaakitanga toward building that just society”. The Chief Justice’s full speech is available on the Courts of NZ website. https://t.co/1AOpB3uLYH", "content_hash": "526815048256fa93e2af6d12d16281f73dc3bea0f4c6aa9bda53562c36fdf94a", "cross_source_ids": {"archive_month": "2021-04", "tweet_id": "1380724743494504451"}, "extraction_method": "internet_archive_cdx_plus_x_oembed", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2021-04-10T00:00:00+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw/x/2021-04/1380724743494504451.json", "record_id": "x:1380724743494504451", "source_account": "CourtsofNZ", "source_kind": "inactive_social_archive", "source_platform": "x", "source_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724743494504451"}
{"agency_id": "courts-nz", "canonical_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724755402170369", "captured_at": "2021-04-10T03:30:27+00:00", "content": "Tā Joe speaks of his vision of a bi-cultural, bi-lingual and bi-jural future for Aotearoa. Justice Williams pays tribute to Governor-General Reddy, who represented the Crown in the Ngāti Pūkenga claim, for journeying to his home marae at Manaia for the ceremony. pic.twitter.com/zOwLVyfxvs", "content_hash": "0e990245f21a6e48b5ae42aa7cf3c96512e543d30ede2d8e9993d3d36aa47b5c", "cross_source_ids": {"archive_month": "2021-04", "tweet_id": "1380724755402170369"}, "extraction_method": "internet_archive_cdx_plus_x_oembed", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2021-04-10T00:00:00+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw/x/2021-04/1380724755402170369.json", "record_id": "x:1380724755402170369", "source_account": "CourtsofNZ", "source_kind": "inactive_social_archive", "source_platform": "x", "source_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724755402170369"}
{"agency_id": "courts-nz", "canonical_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724759936200705", "captured_at": "2021-04-10T03:30:42+00:00", "content": "A wānanga, He Tūruapō-a-iwi: Iwi Visions, follows and will continue into tomorrow. Speakers include Governor-General Dame Patsy Reddy, Minister of Foreign Affairs Nanaia Mahuta, Dame Tariana Turia, and Māori Language Commissioner Professor Rawinia Higgins.", "content_hash": "be6dc94a012a7efa091d2f83efea2439bf6030b2e66896f01fee3f4e3a2ced2b", "cross_source_ids": {"archive_month": "2021-04", "tweet_id": "1380724759936200705"}, "extraction_method": "internet_archive_cdx_plus_x_oembed", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2021-04-10T00:00:00+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw/x/2021-04/1380724759936200705.json", "record_id": "x:1380724759936200705", "source_account": "CourtsofNZ", "source_kind": "inactive_social_archive", "source_platform": "x", "source_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724759936200705"}
{"agency_id": "courts-nz", "canonical_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724767334916097", "captured_at": "2021-04-10T03:30:47+00:00", "content": "Sir Joe invites those at the wānanga to imagine how our systems of government, law, and management could be better. Chief Justice Winkelmann said earlier “That work of imagining and working toward a better society for Aotearoa New Zealand has been the work of Tā Joe’s life”. pic.twitter.com/snUzin94Xs", "content_hash": "516a119ca94ec2f79fa582defd1fce90def355fb47f0ff129e3a8e542ae7334a", "cross_source_ids": {"archive_month": "2021-04", "tweet_id": "1380724767334916097"}, "extraction_method": "internet_archive_cdx_plus_x_oembed", "media_refs": [], "original_created_at": "2021-04-10T00:00:00+00:00", "raw_path": "historical_archive_raw/x/2021-04/1380724767334916097.json", "record_id": "x:1380724767334916097", "source_account": "CourtsofNZ", "source_kind": "inactive_social_archive", "source_platform": "x", "source_url": "https://x.com/CourtsofNZ/status/1380724767334916097"}
